00:33:25.480 --> 00:33:28.034
So this is how we approach the problem.

00:33:28.034 --> 00:33:32.981
Basically said, okay, let's look at how
people are making the decision to drive,

00:33:32.981 --> 00:33:34.106
and when to drive.

00:33:34.106 --> 00:33:38.240
And then we're going to lay out the whole
process of how they make this decision.

00:33:38.240 --> 00:33:39.428
And we'll figure out
when we can intervene.

00:33:39.428 --> 00:33:41.425
Kind of like this hacker mentality, right?

00:33:41.425 --> 00:33:43.710
We figure out,
how is a decision being made?

00:33:43.710 --> 00:33:45.490
And then, where can we insert ourselves?

00:33:45.490 --> 00:33:48.205
And so what we have is drivers
activate their account.

00:33:48.205 --> 00:33:51.942
They set up the preferences for
the number of hours that they work,

00:33:51.942 --> 00:33:55.290
they sign up once a week on
Wednesday to work the next week.

00:33:55.290 --> 00:34:00.030
They get notified of their hours in which
they actually have their hours confirmed.

00:34:00.030 --> 00:34:04.930
They drive and then they get notified for
how much they make while they drive.

00:34:04.930 --> 00:34:10.294
And then if they want they can
pick up hours intermittently.

00:34:10.294 --> 00:34:13.809
So with this flow, what we did is say,

00:34:13.809 --> 00:34:19.151
where are people making the decision
to set their hours, anyone?

00:34:19.151 --> 00:34:19.917
On Wednesday.

00:34:19.917 --> 00:34:24.819
Yep, and where are they learning about how
much money they could make on a Friday

00:34:24.819 --> 00:34:26.590
night over a Tuesday night?

00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:33.806
Not on Wednesday, yep,
two days after they drive.

00:34:33.806 --> 00:34:35.301
So then now this is kind of interesting,
right?

00:34:35.301 --> 00:34:39.145
So we basically say we want to convince
drivers that they should drive on

00:34:39.145 --> 00:34:40.114
a different day.

00:34:40.114 --> 00:34:43.456
But we're telling them about the benefit
of doing it at a completely different

00:34:43.456 --> 00:34:44.528
time, revolutionary.

00:34:44.528 --> 00:34:47.247
But what if we told them about
the benefit of them driving at the point

00:34:47.247 --> 00:34:49.390
they're making a decision?

00:34:49.390 --> 00:34:52.473
So what we did basically is bring
the opportunity cost of their decision on

00:34:52.473 --> 00:34:53.675
the scheduling interface.

00:34:53.675 --> 00:34:55.753
And we said when you're
picking your hours,

00:34:55.753 --> 00:34:59.112
you now know Fridays you can make 35 and
on Tuesdays you make 15.

00:34:59.112 --> 00:35:00.770
My gosh!

00:35:00.770 --> 00:35:01.938
And then we totaled it up for them.

00:35:01.938 --> 00:35:06.008
And so at the end, they had a number
of hours and how much they would make.

00:35:06.008 --> 00:35:09.750
Versus how much on average they could
make if they drove all Fridays.

00:35:09.750 --> 00:35:10.960
We did this in different conditions.

00:35:10.960 --> 00:35:14.360
We said this is very nice, but
what if we actually showed them how much

00:35:14.360 --> 00:35:16.340
gain they could make by
working more Fridays?

00:35:16.340 --> 00:35:19.214
So Fridays had that plus 15, right?

00:35:19.214 --> 00:35:22.317
And so the average was Tuesday and
it was more money on Fridays.

00:35:22.317 --> 00:35:26.020
And so that's also nice, but
we can also show how much they're losing.

00:35:26.020 --> 00:35:31.170
So on Tuesdays we put a minus 15 and
which would work better, right?

00:35:31.170 --> 00:35:32.790
So basically this is how
we think about testing.

00:35:32.790 --> 00:35:35.409
We say okay we have a hypothesis,
we have a theory of change.

00:35:35.409 --> 00:35:39.551
Which is showing people the opportunity
cost at the point of decision is kind of

00:35:39.551 --> 00:35:40.629
our theory, here.

00:35:40.629 --> 00:35:41.620
And we have different tests.

00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:44.232
We have different controls,
we think just showing them is nice.

00:35:44.232 --> 00:35:46.766
But we could probably do ina gain and
a loss and

00:35:46.766 --> 00:35:49.646
then we have a control where
there were no changes.

00:35:49.646 --> 00:35:50.198
Yup.

00:35:50.198 --> 00:35:55.070
&gt;&gt; [INAUDIBLE] but if say I did.

